WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.322 --> 00:00:17.145
washing some doll clothes, Nan and Daisy spread them to dry on the grass.

2
00:00:17.165 --> 00:00:21.668
"Let's climb the willow tree," Nan said.

3
00:00:21.688 --> 00:00:25.050
"We can keep an eye on the clothes so they don't blow away."

4
00:00:27.751 --> 00:00:33.700
That summer the old willow tree had become a favorite spot for everyone to sit and chat.

5
00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:37.484
"I hate washing clothes!"

6
00:00:37.884 --> 00:00:40.526
Nan said as she settled onto a branch.

7
00:00:40.546 --> 00:00:44.970
"Oh, I don't mind washing at all," Daisy said.

8
00:00:44.990 --> 00:00:50.415
"I like cooking and cleaning and anything that has to do with keeping house.

9
00:00:51.756 --> 00:00:56.380
When I grow up, I'll have a nice house where Demi and I can live together."

10
00:00:58.932 --> 00:01:04.194
"Well, I don't have a brother, and I don't want a house to fuss over," Nan said firmly.

11
00:01:04.214 --> 00:01:07.174
"I'll have an office, where I can work as a doctor.

12
00:01:08.415 --> 00:01:11.636
And when my patients are too sick to visit, I'll make house calls.

13
00:01:12.316 --> 00:01:16.237
Curing folks is my idea of fun—not housekeeping!"

14
00:01:16.257 --> 00:01:26.060
"Ugh!" Daisy made a face and asked, "How can you stand those medicines that smell and taste so

15
00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:31.537
nasty?" "As long as I don't have to take them, they don't bother me.

16
00:01:32.797 --> 00:01:34.418
Besides, they make people well.

17
00:01:35.598 --> 00:01:39.899
Mr. Bauer is teaching me the healing properties of the herbs in my garden, and Mrs.

18
00:01:39.939 --> 00:01:42.020
Bauer says I'll be a fine doctor."

19
00:01:43.860 --> 00:01:49.662
Indeed Jo had often mentioned to the professor that Nan had the perfect temperament for a doctor.

20
00:01:51.022 --> 00:01:56.264
She was smart, brave, and felt compassion for anyone sick or in pain.

21
00:01:57.880 --> 00:02:02.004
Jo let Nan assist her whenever any of the boys needed bandaging.

22
00:02:03.525 --> 00:02:07.468
She planned to keep encouraging Nan and her plan to study medicine.

23
00:02:09.610 --> 00:02:14.154
Daisy was still thinking of the more unpleasant aspects of a doctor's life.

24
00:02:14.174 --> 00:02:19.638
"Will you cut off legs and pull out teeth?"

25
00:02:20.619 --> 00:02:21.380
Nan nodded.

26
00:02:21.400 --> 00:02:23.601
"I'll do all those things.

27
00:02:25.223 --> 00:02:29.245
My grandpa was a doctor, and I watched him sew a cut on a man's face.

28
00:02:30.786 --> 00:02:34.367
I helped stop the bleeding, and Grandpa said I was very brave."

29
00:02:34.387 --> 00:02:37.509
"How could you do that?"

30
00:02:38.929 --> 00:02:41.390
Daisy was amazed at her friend's courage.

31
00:02:41.410 --> 00:02:47.873
"I feel sorry for sick people and want to help them, but I shake at the sight of

32
00:02:47.993 --> 00:02:55.037
blood." "You could be my nurse and cuddle my patients when I have to cut off—" "Hey, Nan,

33
00:02:55.097 --> 00:02:56.237
is that you up there?"

34
00:02:56.578 --> 00:02:57.878
called a voice from below.

35
00:02:57.899 --> 00:03:00.700
"I have a splinter in my finger."

36
00:03:02.582 --> 00:03:04.903
Nan looked down and spotted Tommy.

37
00:03:04.923 --> 00:03:08.566
"Climb up, and I'll remove it," she said.

38
00:03:08.586 --> 00:03:12.608
"Though I'm not sure what I'll use for that operation."

39
00:03:15.370 --> 00:03:21.174
By the time Tommy reached them, Daisy had pulled a new packet of sewing needles from her pocket.

40
00:03:21.194 --> 00:03:23.676
"Will one of these work?"

41
00:03:24.016 --> 00:03:24.616
she asked.

42
00:03:24.636 --> 00:03:29.318
"I carry them because I never know when I'll need to mend something."

43
00:03:29.338 --> 00:03:33.940
"Perfect!" Nan said, beaming.

44
00:03:33.960 --> 00:03:37.002
"Maybe you could be my assistant after all."

45
00:03:37.022 --> 00:03:39.183
"No thanks!"

46
00:03:39.683 --> 00:03:44.585
Daisy said, turning her head until Nan had finished removing the splinter.

47
00:03:44.605 --> 00:03:47.326
"All done!"

48
00:03:47.766 --> 00:03:48.407
Nan said.

49
00:03:48.427 --> 00:03:51.448
"Wash your hands, and you'll be good as new."

50
00:03:53.080 --> 00:03:53.781
"Thanks, Nan!"

51
00:03:54.041 --> 00:03:54.761
Tommy said.

52
00:03:54.781 --> 00:03:58.924
"Do you mind if I sit here a minute with you—I'm waiting for Nat."

53
00:04:00.465 --> 00:04:03.206
Nan moved over to make more room for Tommy.

54
00:04:03.226 --> 00:04:05.187
"Hey, Daisy!"

55
00:04:05.668 --> 00:04:06.928
Nat called from below.

56
00:04:06.948 --> 00:04:09.750
"Your doll clothes are blowing away!"

57
00:04:12.852 --> 00:04:19.176
Daisy and Nan climbed down to rescue the clothes, and then Nat climbed up to join Tommy.

58
00:04:20.840 --> 00:04:22.321
"So what did you want to talk to me about?"

59
00:04:22.661 --> 00:04:25.744
Nat asked, settling into Daisy's spot on the branch.

60
00:04:25.764 --> 00:04:31.027
"I've been thinking we should all pool our money and give Dan something to show our respect for

61
00:04:31.067 --> 00:04:32.288
him," Tommy said.

62
00:04:32.308 --> 00:04:36.291
"He was brave to rescue Jack from the birch tree."

63
00:04:36.311 --> 00:04:43.316
"And he was brave to take the blame when everyone suspected me of stealing your money," Nat added.

64
00:04:43.336 --> 00:04:49.080
"Right! Our gift should be something handsome and useful that he'll always remember us by.

65
00:04:50.152 --> 00:04:51.874
So, what do you think I've decided on?"

66
00:04:52.174 --> 00:04:52.995
Tommy asked.

67
00:04:53.015 --> 00:05:00.882
"I know he wants a butterfly net," Nat said hesitantly because he wanted to buy that for Dan

68
00:05:00.922 --> 00:05:08.068
himself. "No, a microscope—a good one that he can peer through and see all kinds of tiny things."

69
00:05:08.088 --> 00:05:14.013
"That's perfect," Nat said, glad that Dan was being appreciated.

70
00:05:14.033 --> 00:05:16.636
"But won't it be expensive?"

71
00:05:17.864 --> 00:05:21.246
"Of course it will, but so far everyone I've asked has contributed.

72
00:05:21.266 --> 00:05:25.449
I've already donated my five dollars," Tommy said.

73
00:05:25.469 --> 00:05:28.251
"All your money?"

74
00:05:28.731 --> 00:05:29.351
Nat said.

75
00:05:29.371 --> 00:05:32.173
"You're the most generous boy I've ever known!"

76
00:05:32.193 --> 00:05:37.497
"Well, I'm tired of the trouble that money causes," Tommy explained.

77
00:05:37.517 --> 00:05:42.460
"From now on, I'm going to give away my cash as fast as I earn it.

78
00:05:43.648 --> 00:05:48.611
That way, no one will try to steal it, and I won't be suspecting innocent people—like you."

79
00:05:48.631 --> 00:05:51.053
"But I thought Mr.

80
00:05:51.113 --> 00:05:53.315
Bauer wanted you to save your money."

81
00:05:53.335 --> 00:05:57.257
"I talked to him, and he thought it was a wonderful plan.

82
00:05:58.418 --> 00:06:02.261
He said some of the best men he knew preferred to do good with their money, rather than

83
00:06:02.341 --> 00:06:03.702
spending it on themselves."

84
00:06:05.283 --> 00:06:08.465
The two boys sat thinking about that for a few minutes.

85
00:06:10.506 --> 00:06:15.818
It was so quiet and peaceful in the tree that Nat wished he'd brought along his violin.

86
00:06:17.019 --> 00:06:19.280
And that soon gave him an idea.

87
00:06:19.300 --> 00:06:23.984
"You know, I don't really need a new violin," Nat said.

88
00:06:24.004 --> 00:06:29.067
"I could buy Dan a butterfly net, and if there's any money left over, I could donate it

89
00:06:29.107 --> 00:06:30.148
to the microscope fund."

90
00:06:30.168 --> 00:06:33.330
"Great!" Tommy said with a grin.

91
00:06:33.350 --> 00:06:35.132
"Let's ask Mr.

92
00:06:35.152 --> 00:06:37.874
Bauer if we can go into town together on Monday afternoon.

93
00:06:38.874 --> 00:06:40.996
You could buy the net while I get the microscope."

94
00:06:42.668 --> 00:06:45.095
"Dan's going to be really surprised!"

95
00:06:45.516 --> 00:06:46.719
Nat said happily.
